Andy Johnson wrote:

> I'm not really sure what you mean about the dots going on the screen at
> 7 Mhz.. can you explain that more? How does it relate to the resolution?
> It sounds like it'd just limit the refresh rate.

A TV has a certain refresh rate, let's call it V refreshes per second.
Now, take this dot clock - 7 Mhz - and divide it by V. There you have the
maximum number of dots that can be transferred in one refresh cycle, which
limits the resolution.

In practice it's even lower, because the electron beam needs time to move
from right to left, and from the bottom of the TV back to the top after a
complete cycle.

